Third-party assets:

The classical Chinese poems quoted in this project are public domain works
(authors died more than 1300 years ago).

The hanging scroll paintings in `src/assets/` are from The Metropolitan
Museum of Art Open Access program and are in the public domain (CC0):
- "Landscape" by Kano Motonobu, 16th century
  https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/45070
- "Landscape" by Unidentified, late 15th century
  https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/829383
- "Mountain Landscape" by Soga Shohaku, ca. 1761-63
  https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/49079
- "Landscape with Pavilion" by Kenko Shokei, 1478-80
  https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/42346
- "Landscape and Couplet of Chinese Verse" by Ike no Taiga, late 18th century
  https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/78153
